# Sherlock Homes Mk2 — rules for AI edits

## Analytical integrity (non-negotiable)
- All findings are computed deterministically in `sherlock/` (pandas/numpy). Never let an LLM compute, choose, or invent a number.
- Never fabricate data, columns or values. Before using a column, check `docs/DATA_DICTIONARY.md` or inspect the file.
- UNKNOWN is a valid result. Do not zero-fill, interpolate or impute missing values unless explicitly asked; if you aggregate or interpolate, label it.
- Never imply causation. Forbidden in generated text: "caused", "led to", "drove", "due to", "because of", "resulted in". Use timing/co-occurrence language ("X increased before Y"; "both increased during this period").
- Never present metro (7-county MSA) or national values as neighborhood measurements. Every value keeps its `geography` label.
- Every calculated value must keep provenance: `source`, `source_id`, `source_file`, `geography`, `period_start`, `period_end`, `time_resolution`.
- Do not compute % change when the base is < 5 (`config.MIN_TOTAL_COUNT`); show n/a.
- Partial years (2019, 2026) are context only — never in change windows.
- New thresholds/method changes must be documented in `docs/METHODOLOGY.md` in the same edit.

## Architecture
- Pipeline: `python -m sherlock.build` → `data/processed/*.json` (+ `web/public/data/` for offline demo).
- API logic lives in `sherlock/service.py`; `api/main.py` stays a thin FastAPI wrapper.
- Frontend types in `web/lib/types.ts` mirror `sherlock/build.py` output — update both together.
- Keep dependencies minimal; geometry is pure Python (`sherlock/geo.py`) — do not add GDAL/GeoPandas unless necessary.
- Run `python -m pytest -q` after changing `sherlock/`; run `npm run typecheck` in `web/` after changing TypeScript.

## Data facts to remember
- Permits changed systems in 2024 (`BUILDING` → `Building & Development Application`, new work_type labels); use the crosswalk in `sherlock/ingest.py`.
- Permits have no dwelling-unit count; permit ≠ completed housing.
- City-owned vacant lots are a snapshot of City-owned parcels only — not a vacancy rate.
- Zillow file `9a1c60bd-...csv` is *inferred* ZHVI — keep the "inferred" label.
- Mk2 ZIP layer: Zillow ZHVI/ZORI + County VALID sales (2020+ only). ZIP values must be labelled ZIP-level and never presented as neighborhood values.
- Rent window is Aug 2023 → Aug 2026 (ZORI coverage); keep that label.
- No income, population or vacancy-rate data is loaded unless data/raw/acs/acs_<year>.json exists.
- Dr. John (sherlock/drjohn.py) must keep citations ([D#] Sherlock data, [W#] web) and the verification step; web text must never be presented as Sherlock data.
